{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"code":"POST \/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift#L83","fileName":"MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Mixpanel’s limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON array of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first, each with two members: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s stored properties by name, then these members:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; left out for a record with no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds it; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0\""},{"type":"text","text":", so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The project token"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and no other device","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its unique users are sessions. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own anonymous user, linked to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing, rather than an event with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Mixpanel would attribute to no user,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or to a hash of the request’s address. Mixpanel treats two events of the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as one, so a recovered record that Mixpanel had already stored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under its session, before the app ended, is stored again. The record’s vendor identifier and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel cuts each string down to 255 characters. It drops an event of 255 properties or more,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counting the members above and the default properties below, one holding an array of 255"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements or more, and one whose property nests objects more than 3 deep, though it answers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"200: the encoder enforces these limits, leaving such a record out of the request."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"text":" also holds Mixpanel’s default properties, named as its Swift SDK names them, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$app_version_string","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$app_build_number","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The version and build, each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$wifi"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ do, one with a property named as one Mixpanel reads for itself,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one past Mixpanel’s limits on properties, array elements or nesting, one whose event isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Mixpanel takes, and one too large for Mixpanel (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logs and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it. Mixpanel answers a request it reads with 200, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" retries one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400, 401 or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"413. Mixpanel answers 200 as well when it ingests none of a request’s events: a wrong region,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored, so check the project’s Live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"View after setting it up. Its track API ingests only events from the last 5 days: a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"older than that when it is sent, such as one a store kept through a long time offline, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted as delivered and not stored. A record sent again keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The bytes are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same for the same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\